    {
      "title": "Pope Leo’s recovery from lung cancer surgery ‘progressing as planned’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/14/pope-leo-recovery-lung-cancer-surgery-progressing-as-planned",
      "description": "<p>Pontiff has begun walking in his hospital room and is eating normally after operation to remove growth, doctors say</p><p>Pope Leo’s recovery from a lung cancer operation is progressing as planned, his doctors have said, as the pontiff received good wishes from around the world, including from Britain’s King Charles.</p><p>Leo, who had a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/13/pope-leo-hospital-operation-growth-lung\">cancerous mass removed from his right lung</a> late on Tuesday, began walking in his hospital room after respiratory therapy on Wednesday. He was eating normally, his doctors Luigi Carbone and Stefano Margaritoria said in a statement issued by the Vatican.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/14/pope-leo-recovery-lung-cancer-surgery-progressing-as-planned\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-14T22:31:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "As Pope Leo Recovers From Surgery, Messages of Support Abound at Rome Hospital",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/14/world/europe/pope-leo-surgery-cancer-hospital-rome.html",
      "description": "The pontiff, 71, is expected to spend about a week in the hospital recovering from surgery that found lung cancer. Messages of support have flooded in from far and wide.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-10-14T15:42:26"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pope Leo Is in ‘Good Mood’ After Cancer Surgery, Vatican Says: What to Know",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/14/world/europe/pope-leo-xiv-cancer-diagnosis.html",
      "description": "Pope Leo XIV was diagnosed with a common form of lung cancer. The Vatican said that he was walking and receiving therapy after an operation to remove a cancerous nodule.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-10-14T16:32:23"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pope Leo’s Cancer Surgery Draws Outpouring From World Leaders",
